# fritzlog rules: which FRITZ!Box event log entries are expected.
#
#   category   color   pattern
#
# category: a-z, 0-9 and _, at most 16 characters; it names the RRD file
#           fritzlog,<category>.rrd (new entries per poll).
# color:    green (only counted), yellow or red (the column keeps that
#           color for FRITZBOX_HOLD_MINUTES after the entry appears).
# pattern:  POSIX extended regular expression (awk), the rest of the
#           line, matched against the message text without the time.
#
# The first matching rule wins. An entry no rule matches is "unmatched"
# and turns the column yellow (FRITZBOX_LOG_UNMATCHED_COLOR): Xymon then
# records it, and a rule for it can be added here.
#
# The box writes its log in the language of its user interface; these
# rules are for German. Patterns stay ASCII: an umlaut is two bytes in
# the box's UTF-8 text, so ".*" stands in for it (Pr.*fix = Praefix).
# All rules below match messages seen on a FRITZ!Box 7510, FRITZ!OS 8.26.

# Daily reconnect that pre-empts the provider's forced disconnect.
reconnect   green   Zwangstrennung durch den Anbieter
# Internet connection established or lost (IPv4 and IPv6). The current
# state is reported by fritzdsl/fritzwan; the log entries are only counted.
wan_up      green   ^Internetverbindung (IPv6 )?wurde erfolgreich hergestellt
wan_down    green   ^Internetverbindung (IPv6 )?wurde getrennt
# IPv6 prefix obtained or renewed.
ipv6_prefix green   ^IPv6-Pr.*fix wurde erfolgreich (bezogen|aktualisiert)
# A SIP registration or call setup failed.
voip_fail   yellow  ^Internettelefonie mit .* war nicht erfolgreich
